#: ../../content/applications/services/timesheets/logging_time.rst:3
msgid "Logging time"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/services/timesheets/logging_time.rst:5
msgid "Besides the standard list, grid, and Kanban views, time can be recorded and reviewed in a calendar, and it can be attached to the activities of the :doc:`Activities </applications/essentials/activities>` app."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/services/timesheets/logging_time.rst:12
msgid "Calendar view"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/services/timesheets/logging_time.rst:14
msgid "The timesheet lists offer a :icon:`fa-calendar` :guilabel:`Calendar` view, which opens by default on :menuselection:`Timesheets --> Timesheets --> All Timesheets` and on the timesheets of a project. Entries are placed on the day they were logged, sized by the time spent, and colored by project."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/services/timesheets/logging_time.rst:19
msgid "Use the :guilabel:`Month`, :guilabel:`Week`, and :guilabel:`Day` scales to see a whole month at a glance or a single day in detail, and the side panel to filter by :guilabel:`Employee`, :guilabel:`Project`, :guilabel:`Task`, or :guilabel:`User`. The total of the displayed time is shown with the entries, and an entry with an impossible duration — more than 24 hours, or a negative one — is highlighted, which makes mistyped entries easy to spot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/services/timesheets/logging_time.rst:25
msgid "The timesheet analysis report can be displayed in the same way, so the recorded costs and hours can be reviewed per employee on a calendar."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/services/timesheets/logging_time.rst:29
msgid "The calendar views are provided by the *Timesheet Calendar View* (`timesheet_view_calendar`) module."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/services/timesheets/logging_time.rst:43
msgid "Time spent on activities"
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/services/timesheets/logging_time.rst:45
msgid "Timesheet entries can be linked to an :guilabel:`Activity`, so that the time spent on a planned piece of work is recorded against that activity rather than only against the task. Each entry can additionally carry a :guilabel:`Start Date` and an :guilabel:`End Date`, which is useful when the exact interval matters, for example for interventions billed by the hour."
msgstr ""

#: ../../content/applications/services/timesheets/logging_time.rst:50
msgid "The activity then shows:"
